@startuml textbook-strategy
title Strategy Pattern - Textbook Reference Structure\n(Reproduced from Java OO Design Patterns, HanbitDP chapter 5, figure 5-5)
top to bottom direction
skinparam classFontSize 12
skinparam classBorderThickness 1.2
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam dpi 130
hide empty members
hide circle

class Robot <<Context>> #FFD0D0 {
  -name: String
  +move()
  +attack()
  +setMovingStrategy(s)
  +setAttackStrategy(s)
}

interface MovingStrategy <<Strategy>> {
  +move()
}
interface AttackStrategy <<Strategy>> {
  +attack()
}

together {
  class WalkingStrategy
  class FlyingStrategy
}
together {
  class PunchStrategy
  class MissileStrategy
}

class Atom
class TaekwonV

Robot --> "1" MovingStrategy : uses
Robot --> "1" AttackStrategy : uses
Robot <|-- Atom
Robot <|-- TaekwonV
MovingStrategy <|.. WalkingStrategy
MovingStrategy <|.. FlyingStrategy
AttackStrategy <|.. PunchStrategy
AttackStrategy <|.. MissileStrategy

note right of Robot
  Maps to GoF "Context" role.
  Injects the chosen strategy at runtime
  via setMovingStrategy / setAttackStrategy.
end note
@enduml
